     The alert notifications' colour: the error role, so alerts stay red
     and match the system's error colour. The notification shade keeps it
     legible in light and dark theme itself.

     Nothing else in the overlayable group is changed: the four themes
     already build on DeviceDefault and SettingsLib themes, so they take the
     dynamic colours as they are; cell_broadcast_color_primary and
     cell_broadcast_color_primary_dark are not used by the app; the alert
     dimensions are layout, not colour; the red extreme-alert icon is not
     overlayable and stays. No booleans, arrays or strings.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="notification_color">@android:color/system_error_light</color>
</resources>
